<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · artifact</p><h1 class="enc-title">Motya Charioteer</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 470 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/5th-century-bce">5th century BCE</a> · Also known as Youth of Motya, Mozia Charioteer</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Motya Charioteer is a marble statue of a young man in a long, finely pleated tunic, found in 1979 on the island of Motya off western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sicily">Sicily</a>. Carved by a Greek sculptor in about 470 to 450 BCE, it is one of the finest surviving works of the early Classical style. Its subject and how it reached a Phoenician city are debated; it is displayed in the Whitaker Museum on the island.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/motya-charioteer.jpg" alt="Motya Charioteer" width="320" height="427" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Ismoon 18:04, 15 August 2022 (UTC) · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Aurige_de_Mozia_de_face-2.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
